---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Kit - Julian Codespoti"
  description="The small Astro + MDX component kit used to build interactive articles on this site."
  activeNav="framework"
>
  <main class="col-page">
    <h1 class="page-title">Interactive Article Kit</h1>
    <p class="page-sub">
      A small set of Astro + MDX primitives for writing technical articles with simple, interactive diagrams.
    </p>

    <div class="essay-prose">
      <p>
        Prose compiles to plain static HTML with zero JavaScript. Each diagram is a small React island mounted with
        <code>client:visible</code> so pages stay fast and animations pause offscreen.
      </p>

      <h2>Primitives in <code>src/kit/</code></h2>
      <ul>
        <li><code>&lt;Legend color="amber"&gt;code&lt;/Legend&gt;</code> places an inline colored square right inside a sentence so prose and diagrams share one visual vocabulary without legends cluttering the box.</li>
        <li><code>&lt;Diagram&gt;</code> wraps a single visual in a flat bordered well with an optional header strip and bottom control bar.</li>
        <li><code>&lt;TimelineSlider&gt;</code> gives any multi-step visual a reset button, prev/next buttons, and a scrubbable range bar with discrete ticks.</li>
        <li><code>&lt;ModeSwitch&gt;</code> provides a flat two-choice toggle for comparing a broken behavior against its fix.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Adding a new article</h2>
      <p>Drop a new <code>.mdx</code> file into <code>src/content/essays/</code>, put its diagram components in <code>src/sims/</code>, and push to <code>main</code>.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
